    "title": "Mayor Ellis responds to Monroe City Council - NewsBreak",
    "text": "MONROE, La – (KTVE/KARD) It has been 13 months since the city of Monroe has had a confirmed Fire Chief. Delays over appointing a new chief have come from disputes between Mayor Friday Ellis and the City Council members. Every other council before this council has always respected the relationship between the department head and the mayor. They may not have liked it, but they but they haven’t voted down these folks because they understand and respected the process. Mayor Ellis says that the next steps in appointing a Chief will be to let Governor Landry make the decision. This was put in place for when the two parties cannot come to a decision. Governor Landry is currently on leave after the passing of his father and is expected to make a decision at some point after he returns. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KTVE - myarklamiss.com.",
